        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>START HERE</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;text-wrap:balance;color:#0f172a'>Your first graph</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:italic 400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.35 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#475569'>Nodes, and how they relate. This one is yours: change anything.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>What to do first</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><span style='float:left;padding:6px 10px 0 0;font:500 68px/54px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'>T</span>he three nodes on the stage are an example. Move them, rename them, or delete them when you are ready.</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><strong>Resize a node</strong> by dragging its corner. Double-click a node to go inside it.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><strong>Connect two nodes</strong> by dragging from a handle on one to the other. The name on the edge says how they relate.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><strong>Right-click</strong> for Properties: the graph&#39;s own, a node&#39;s, or an edge&#39;s.</li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><strong>Save</strong> from the Document menu, which also keeps your History.</li></ul></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='primary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:12px;border-top:3px solid #6d28d9'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 26px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>Start here</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>A short walk through making a graph.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/tutorial/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#6d28d9'>Open the tutorial →</a></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 22px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>What a graph is</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>The root of every graph, and what it holds.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/primitives/root/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#475569'>Read about it →</a></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='secondary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 22px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>The Twilite Zone</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>Where graphs like this one live, and how they link.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#475569'>Open the Zone →</a></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>The root</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Every graph has exactly one root. It holds the graph&#39;s name and description, says what kind of graph it is, and is where every other part connects.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>The masthead</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The title and the one line under it, at the top of the page. Change its words and the page redraws.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>A section</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A heading and a body, like this one. Copy a section and the copy joins the page, in graph order.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>A route</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A link from the page to another graph. Routes that follow one another share a row; point one at any graph by its address.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>The views and the glyph</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The Detail is the page in full. The Summary is the same page as a card, for when the graph is seen smaller. The glyph is the mark for when it is seen smallest.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>The environment</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>This poster is the graph&#39;s environment: the room its work sits in. Delete it and the graph stands on plain graph paper.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>The Method</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Assemble the page reads the masthead, the sections and the routes and writes the Detail and Summary views, every time the graph changes.</p></section></div></div></div>"
        },
